<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO unit sells remaining stake in CMG.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO unit sells remaining stake in CMG.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Dutch computer services company Computer Management Group Plc (CMG) said on Thursday that AMRO Participaties BV had sold its total holding of 3.211.395 ordinary CMG shares representing five percent of the ordinary share capital.</p>
<p>&quot;These shares were placed with ten institutions in London and Amsterdam,&quot; CMG said in a statement. The identity of the buyers was not disclosed.</p>
<p>ABN AMRO Participaties, a venture capital unit of bank ABN AMRO, sold a 2.2 percent stake in CMG in September 1996.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
